From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: pd-mapper: describe the exact Uke OEM domains

The pinned Uke Global OS3.0.304.0 modem image contains adspr, adsps,
adspua, battmgr and cdspr service registries. Their domain names,
instances and services exactly match these existing mainline entries.
Use a Uke-only match; do not infer mappings for other SM7675 devices.
This advertises service locations, not FastRPC memory permissions or
automatic remote-processor startup.

--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_pd_mapper.c
@@ -582,1 +582,11 @@
+/* Exact domains from Uke's OEM service registries. */
+static const struct qcom_pdm_domain_data *uke_domains[] = {
+	&adsp_audio_pd,
+	&adsp_root_pd,
+	&adsp_charger_pd,
+	&adsp_sensor_pd,
+	&cdsp_root_pd,
+	NULL,
+};
+
 static const struct of_device_id qcom_pdm_domains[] __maybe_unused = {
@@ -630,2 +640,3 @@
-	{},
+	{ .compatible = "xiaomi,uke", .data = uke_domains, },
+	{},
 };
